WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.660
In the early decades of the 20th century the discovery of something called antimatter

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.080
raised a significant problem.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.880
This new substance called into question how our matter filled universe could exist at all. Let me explain.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:24.060
In 1928 Paul Dirac came up with a new and elegant equation to describe how particles like electrons

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.660
behave when they travel close to the speed of light.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:36.680
Surprisingly, Dirac found that his equation always had two solutions--sort of how the square root of a positive number always has

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.780
two answers.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:44.560
Dirac recognized that one solution described the electron but the other... well, that was a mystery,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.760
which he first dismissed as a mathematical artifact.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.719
He later said it took him three tortured years to summon the courage

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.128
to claim that this other set of solutions was describing something real:

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:03.900
Antimatter.   That is, the first solution described an electron while the second described an anti-electron.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.800
The anti-electron would have the same mass and spin as the electron, but it would have an

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.780
opposite electric charge.  Now since the electron has a negative charge,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.140
the anti-electron would have a positive charge, which is why we also call it a positron.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.720
Dirac's equation says the same thing is true for all particles.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:32.480
Quarks have anti quarks, and just as quarks can make up protons, anti-quarks can make up anti-protons, and anti-protons

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.620
and anti-electrons, they can make anti-atoms, and so on.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.620
Dirac's theory was a remarkable achievement.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.140
If proven incorrect, it would double the number of known particles in the world.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.760
Just four years later in

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.700
1932, Carl Anderson took this picture of a particle

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.900
racing through a bubble chamber.  His measurements showed that it had the same mass as an electron, but a positive electric charge,

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.040
the first detection of antimatter

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.020
verifying Dirac's mathematical prediction.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:11.080
Now we come to the puzzle; when matter and antimatter come together,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:17.360
they annihilate, and this raises a big question.  Why is there any matter left?

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.700
After all, if matter and antimatter are

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:28.240
identical except for having opposite electric charge, and since as far as we can tell, the laws of physics don't have a preference for a

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:35.640
plus sign over a minus sign, we would expect equal amounts of matter and antimatter to be created at the Big Bang.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:44.280
And then as they intermingled, the matter and antimatter would all annihilate, leaving a sea of structureless radiation.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.620
But if this were the case, the universe as we know it wouldn't exist.

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:52.319
So what's going on?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.410
Physicists have been puzzling about this for more than half a century.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.899
Some have wondered whether the antimatter got separated from matter and might still be out there,

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:08.519
existing as anti-planets, anti-stars, anti-galaxies, maybe even anti-universes.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:11.849
Others have imagined that just after the Big Bang,

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:15.119
a tiny imbalance between matter and antimatter

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.880
somehow crept in.   Indeed, to avoid total annihilation,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.920
scientists have calculated that for every billion anti-protons,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.820
there must have been a billion plus one protons.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:35.300
That's a tiny imbalance, but it would have left over just enough matter to make all we see in the universe today.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.480
To figure out which, if any, of these theories might be right,

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:45.929
scientists are undertaking a range of experiments to understand antimatter with far greater precision, and

00:03:46.269 --> 00:03:52.969
all this is part of a grand quest to answer a question that as simple as it is profound.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:58.699
Given that matter and antimatter annihilate, how is it that we exist?

